---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Honest Picture's privacy policy: how we handle data, cookies, analytics, and advertising (Google AdSense), and the rights you have under the GDPR and CCPA. Your assessment answers never leave your browser."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  eyebrow="Trust & Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lede="The short version: your assessment answers never leave your browser, we do not require an account, and we are transparent about the limited data the site does collect — including cookies used for analytics and advertising."
  updated="July 2026"
>
  <h2>The principle</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} ("{SITE.name}," "we," "us," or "our") is built so that the most
    sensitive thing you do here — answering honest questions about your life —
    happens entirely on your own device. We designed it this way on purpose. A
    site about seeing your life clearly should not quietly harvest it. This policy
    explains, in plain language, what information the site does and does not
    collect, how it is used, who it may be shared with, and the choices and legal
    rights you have.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy applies to <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a> (the "site") and
    covers our assessment tool, our research library, and the rest of the site. By
    using the site, you agree to the practices described here.
  </p>

  <h2>Your assessment answers (processed only in your browser)</h2>
  <p>
    The Context Assessment is a client-side application. This is the core of our
    privacy design:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your answers are processed <strong>only in your browser</strong> to generate your context picture.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not stored</strong> on our servers, in a database, or in your browser's local storage.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not transmitted</strong> to us or to any third party.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not linked</strong> to your identity, because we never ask for it and we do not require an account.</li>
    <li>When you close or refresh the page, your answers are gone.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The <a href="/reality-check">Daily Reality Check</a> game works the same way:
    your guess and streak are kept only on your own device (in your browser's
    local storage, so the page can remember you played today) and are never
    transmitted to us or anyone else. Clearing your browser data removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>Beyond the assessment, the site collects only a limited set of standard information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you choose to give us.</strong> If you email us, we
      receive your email address and whatever you include in your message. We use
      it only to respond.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like virtually every
      website, our hosting provider and analytics may record standard technical
      data: your IP address, approximate (city/country-level) location derived
      from it, browser and device type, operating system, referring page, and the
      pages you view. This is used for security, reliability, and aggregate
      analytics — never to build a profile of you by name.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookies and similar technologies.</strong> Small files and
      equivalents may be stored on your device for the purposes described in the
      next two sections.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file a website stores on your device. We (and our
    service providers) may use the following categories:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Strictly necessary cookies.</strong> Needed for the site to function
      and to remember basic preferences (such as a consent choice). These do not
      require consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics cookies.</strong> Help us understand aggregate, largely
      anonymised usage — which pages are read and roughly how many people visit —
      so we can improve the site. See <em>Analytics</em> below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising cookies.</strong> Set by Google and other third-party
      advertising partners to serve and measure ads. See <em>Advertising and
      Google AdSense</em> below.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings, and, where
    required by law, we will ask for your consent before setting non-essential
    (analytics or advertising) cookies. Blocking some cookies may affect how parts
    of the site work.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    This site is supported in part by advertising served through
    <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, an advertising service provided by Google LLC.
    To fund the free research library, we display ads, and this involves the
    following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, <strong>including Google</strong>, use cookies to serve
      ads based on your prior visits to this website and other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads
      to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      These cookies may collect data such as your IP address, device identifiers,
      and browsing activity to help show more relevant ads and measure their
      performance. We do not receive or store this data ourselves, and we never
      share your assessment answers with advertisers — those answers never leave
      your browser.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can control the ads you see and opt out of personalised advertising:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Manage Google's ad personalisation at
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Opt out of personalised advertising from many vendors at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a>
      (US) or
      <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (EU).
    </li>
    <li>
      Review how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where required (for example, for visitors in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland), we
    use a consent mechanism so that non-essential advertising and analytics cookies
    are set only after you agree, and you can change your choice at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use a privacy-conscious analytics service (such as Google Analytics or a
    similar tool) to understand aggregate traffic. Analytics data is used only in
    aggregate, is not combined with your assessment answers, and is not used to
    identify you personally. Where the tool supports it, we enable IP anonymisation.
    You can opt out of Google Analytics using
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    See <a href="/how-we-use-data">how we use data</a> for specifics.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate, maintain, secure, and improve the site.</li>
    <li>To respond to your emails and requests.</li>
    <li>To understand aggregate usage and make the content better.</li>
    <li>To display advertising that helps fund the site.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal bases (for EEA/UK visitors)</h2>
  <p>
    Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on: your <strong>consent</strong>
    (for non-essential cookies and advertising/analytics); our
    <strong>legitimate interests</strong> in running and securing the site and
    responding to you; and <strong>legal obligation</strong> where applicable. You
    may withdraw consent at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>How information is shared</h2>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share limited data
    only with service providers who help us run the site, under contracts that
    limit their use of it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting and content delivery</strong> (to serve the site and keep security logs).</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics providers</strong> (aggregate usage).</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising partners</strong>, including Google, as described above.</li>
    <li>Where required by law, or to protect the rights, safety, and security of the site and its users.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep information only as long as needed for the purpose it was collected.
    Email correspondence is retained until it is no longer needed and then deleted
    on request. Server logs and analytics are retained for limited periods
    consistent with security and standard provider defaults. Your assessment
    answers are never retained at all, because they are never collected.
  </p>

  <h2>International data transfers</h2>
  <p>
    The site is operated from, and its providers may process data in, the United
    States and other countries. Where personal data is transferred internationally,
    we rely on appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses) offered
    by our providers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not build profiles or store your answers, there is usually no
    personal dataset about you for us to export or delete. Depending on where you
    live, you may still have rights over any information we do hold (such as email
    correspondence):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>EEA/UK (GDPR):</strong> the right to access, correct, delete, restrict,
      or object to processing, to data portability, and to withdraw consent or lodge
      a complaint with your local data protection authority.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>California (CCPA/CPRA):</strong> the right to know what personal
      information is collected and how it is used, to request deletion, to correct
      it, to opt out of "sale" or "sharing" of personal information, and not to be
      discriminated against for exercising these rights. We do not sell personal
      information.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any right, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    and we will respond within the time required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is intended for adults and is not directed at children under 13 (or
    the applicable minimum age in your jurisdiction, such as 16 in parts of the EU).
    We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a
    child has provided us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    Because there is no common industry standard for Do Not Track (DNT), we do not
    respond to DNT signals. Where required, we honour recognised opt-out signals
    such as Global Privacy Control (GPC) for the "sale"/"sharing" of personal
    information.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect information,
    including serving the site over HTTPS and minimising what we collect. No method
    of transmission or storage is perfectly secure, but collecting as little as
    possible is our strongest safeguard.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Our pages link to external sources, studies, and services. We are not
    responsible for the privacy practices of those sites; please review their own
    policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the site evolves or as laws change. Material
    changes will be reflected in the "last updated" date above, and, where required,
    we will provide additional notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy, or want to exercise a right? Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. For related detail, see
    <a href="/how-we-use-data">how we use data</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
